This group has featured many a (deserved) tribute to the dev team.
Tonight, I'm in a bad mood, and I feel like pointing out the 10
worst (mis)features in the game.  Here goes....

 10) Corpses intermingle in your inventory.  Accidentally carry around
     an old jackal corpse, kill a fresh one, pick it up and eat it...
     oops - the two are intermingled and you get very sick
 
  9) Bags are painful to use.  The user interface should be the same
     as normal inventory - merely select the item to insert or remove
     from the bag.

  8) Hitting <escape> when a priest asks you for a contribution should
     abort the transaction, not give him all your gold!

  7) Drinking from a sink should never result in the "pipes break"
     scenario - but kicking it should have a chance to do so.

  6) The "\" command should show the potions/scrolls/etc. in the order
     they were discovered.  This prevents a rathy nasty form of abuse.

  5) The "effect" generated when a bolt/ray hits a resistant creature
     takes WAY too long.  Walk into a roomful of liches wearing a ring
     of conflict, and be prepared to be bored to death.

  4) Moving into a pool should require confirmation ala "safe pet".
     Cmon guys, this is not a contest to see who doesn't have a
     system with keybounce or occasional slow response!

  3) Normal speed monsters should not be able to pick up a knife
     (or whatever) and throw it on the same move.

  2) The forced name change on a polymorph is a stinker.  On a large
     system, where people play with their login name, they want their
     name to appear on the scoreboard - not to mention the novice's
     problem with game restart.

  1) Worst of all!  Despite the above 9 gripes, the game is so good
     that I waste far too much time playing it!


